    {"cmc":3.0,"color_identity":["B"],"colors":["B"],"defense":null,"keywords":["Hexproof"],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{2}{B}","name":"Xathrid Slyblade","oracle_id":"931c0cd3-06fb-42da-86f2-476d08a238f9","oracle_text":"Hexproof (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control.)\n{3}{B}: Until end of turn, this creature loses hexproof and gains first strike and deathtouch. (It deals combat damage before creatures without first strike. Any amount of damage it deals to a creature is enough to destroy it.)","power":"2","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2014-07-18","toughness":"1","type_line":"Creature — Human Assassin"}
  ],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"A spell cast using flashback will always be exiled afterward, whether it resolves, is countered, or leaves the stack in some other way.","oracle_id":"195c6453-e5cc-4b3b-8518-eaccf29bc4a6","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a card with flashback is put into your graveyard during your turn, you can cast it if it’s legal to do so before any other player can take any actions.","oracle_id":"195c6453-e5cc-4b3b-8518-eaccf29bc4a6","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"To determine the total cost of a spell, start with the mana cost or alternative cost (such as a flashback cost) you’re paying, add any cost increases, then apply any cost reductions. The mana value of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was.","oracle_id":"195c6453-e5cc-4b3b-8518-eaccf29bc4a6","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You can cast a spell using flashback even if it was somehow put into your graveyard without having been cast.","oracle_id":"195c6453-e5cc-4b3b-8518-eaccf29bc4a6","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You must still follow any timing restrictions and permissions, including those based on the card’s type. For instance, you can cast a sorcery using flashback only when you could normally cast a sorcery.","oracle_id":"195c6453-e5cc-4b3b-8518-eaccf29bc4a6","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"“Flashback [cost]” means “You may cast this card from your graveyard by paying [cost] rather than paying its mana cost” and “If the flashback cost was paid, exile this card instead of putting it anywhere else any time it would leave the stack.”","oracle_id":"195c6453-e5cc-4b3b-8518-eaccf29bc4a6","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"In a Limited event (usually Booster Draft or Sealed Deck), you can't add basic snow lands to your card pool as you would other basic lands. You can play with basic snow lands only if you open them in your sealed deck or draft them.","oracle_id":"5b2460a5-6ae5-4cad-ba94-1a9e98e6e4c0","published_at":"2021-02-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Snow is a supertype, not a card type. It has no rules meaning or function by itself, but spells and abilities may refer to it.","oracle_id":"5b2460a5-6ae5-4cad-ba94-1a9e98e6e4c0","published_at":"2021-02-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Snow isn't a type of mana. If an effect says you may spend mana as though it were any type, you can't pay for {S} using mana that wasn't produced by a snow source.","oracle_id":"5b2460a5-6ae5-4cad-ba94-1a9e98e6e4c0","published_at":"2021-02-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Some cards have additional effects for each {S} spent to cast them. You can cast these spells even if you don't spend any snow mana to cast them; their additional effects simply won't do anything.","oracle_id":"5b2460a5-6ae5-4cad-ba94-1a9e98e6e4c0","published_at":"2021-02-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The Kaldheim set doesn't have any cards with mana costs that include {S}, but some previous sets do. If an effect says such a spell costs {1} less to cast, that reduction doesn't apply to any {S} costs. This is also true for activated abilities that include {S} in their activation costs and effects that reduce those costs.","oracle_id":"5b2460a5-6ae5-4cad-ba94-1a9e98e6e4c0","published_at":"2021-02-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The {S} symbol is a generic mana symbol. It represents a cost that can be paid by one mana that was produced by a snow source. That mana can be any color or colorless.","oracle_id":"5b2460a5-6ae5-4cad-ba94-1a9e98e6e4c0","published_at":"2021-02-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A landfall ability doesn't trigger if a permanent already on the battlefield becomes a land.","oracle_id":"8a1d14c2-ca31-4711-b385-f4af0c1c0b04","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A landfall ability triggers whenever a land you control enters for any reason. It triggers whenever you play a land, as well as whenever a spell or ability puts a land onto the battlefield under your control.","oracle_id":"8a1d14c2-ca31-4711-b385-f4af0c1c0b04","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Whenever a land you control enters, each landfall ability of the permanents you control will trigger. You can put them   on the stack in any order. The last ability you put on the stack will be the first one to resolve (As a result, you can have those abilities resolve in the order of your choosing.).","oracle_id":"8a1d14c2-ca31-4711-b385-f4af0c1c0b04","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not modal. If the target changes from an artifact to an enchantment or vice versa, this still destroys it.","oracle_id":"a7e97fa9-4b72-4548-b854-5be5f18a6f1a","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Can be used on a creature without Flying with no effect.","oracle_id":"c9ffce6c-a113-4c9d-9148-5ace68f68793","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Damage dealt to a creature with indestructible is still marked on that creature. If that creature loses indestructible, and the marked damage is lethal, it will be destroyed. However, if a creature with indestructible is dealt damage by a source with deathtouch and then later loses indestructible, that creature won’t be destroyed.","oracle_id":"d93ba2f2-bf9b-444b-adbb-3835662734e7","published_at":"2016-01-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The last ability causes creatures your opponents control to lose hexproof and indestructible as it resolves. Effects that cause those creatures to gain those abilities after that point will work normally.","oracle_id":"d93ba2f2-bf9b-444b-adbb-3835662734e7","published_at":"2016-01-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"To work as an evasion ability, an attacking creature must already have flying when the declare blockers step begins. Once a creature has become blocked, giving it flying won’t change that.","oracle_id":"f7518456-45ed-41d4-bd3c-5aacea28eb35","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
